      "artist": "Kate Jewell",
      "description": "A place to hide. The Major Oak is hollow and 40 years ago it was possible to squeeze inside. The successful remedial management of the tree, (see 1330600), including the anti fungal paint on the edge of the hole, means it would be a very tight squeeze today.",
